 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "The proof is pointwise length scaling followed by `ENNReal.mul_iInf_of_ne` twice and `lintegral_const_mul'`; none of these steps needs \u211d. `Scaling.lean` has `mgradient_rescale_const` (line 196), `laplaceBeltrami_rescale_const` and the curvature rescaling lemmas, but no norm, length or distance lemma. Grepping `TauCeti/Geometry` for `(riemannianEDist|pathELength).*(rescale|smul|const)` finds only unrelated `pathELength_riemannianExp_smul` lemmas.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Morse/Examples/MetricRescaling.lean",
   "fix": "Add `ContMDiffRiemannianMetric.riemannianEDist_rescale_const` (and `pathELength_rescale_const`) to `TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Riemannian/Scaling.lean`, in the `letI` style of `mgradient_rescale_const`: for any `g : ContMDiffRiemannianMetric I n E (fun x : M \u21a6 TangentSpace I x)` and `0 < c`, the distance of `g.rescale (fun _ \u21a6 c) \u2026` between x and y equals `ENNReal.ofReal \u221ac * riemannianEDist I x y` for `g`. Then derive the line case from it and the `IsRiemannianManifold` instance for \u211d, and drop the line-specific helper.",
   "issue": "`riemannianEDist_scaledLineMetric` (with its helper `eNorm_scaledLineMetric`, ~line 93) proves only for \u211d that rescaling a metric by a constant c > 0 scales every tangent-vector length, and hence `riemannianEDist`, by \u221ac. The proof uses nothing about \u211d beyond the final step identifying the standard distance with |x - y|.",
   "line": 158
  }
 ],
